-- An action is a pattern: `Sign t` binds a NEW `t` matching any signer, which
-- would let a stranger's signature discharge tenant t's duty. The checker
-- refuses the silent shadowing and says to write `Sign (EXACTLY t)`.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Tenant HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign HAS signer IS AN Actor

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
bad MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t MUST Sign t WITHIN 14
